export default {"name":"metre-customer-service-rag","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"overview-metre","title":"Metre (一米通) — what it is","text":"Metre (一米通), operated by Metre Hong Kong Limited (一米通有限公司), is a Hong Kong parking and access-control company. It provides an Ultra-Wideband (UWB) electronic ID (e-ID) validation system. The product family is MetreTag (a small UWB device installed in the vehicle), MetrePoint (the UWB reader / barrier at the car-park entrance) and the Metre App (一手通 App). Drivers drive near a MetrePoint and the barrier rises automatically; parking fees are paid in the app with FPS (轉數快).","keywords":["metre","一米通","uwb","e-id","electronic id","泊車","停車場","metretag","metrepoint","metre app","一手通","fps","轉數快","access control","門禁"],"category":"overview","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"overview-why","title":"Why Metre exists — the problem it solves","text":"Traditional licence-plate recognition (LPR / 車牌識別) can fail because of dirt, weather, lighting, angles or obstruction, which causes driver complaints and barrier delays. Metre replaces plate recognition with Ultra-Wideband (UWB) identification: the tag is recognised at centimetre-level range with tamper-resistant signalling, so the barrier rises automatically as the car approaches and no action is required from the driver. UWB also protects privacy because a vehicle can be whitelisted with a Metre ID instead of a licence plate, and the e-ID is stored in a secure element. For car-park operators the system is low-cost because the e-ID lives on the driver's phone or a small tag, and it removes the need to upgrade existing gate hardware.","keywords":["why","problem","licence plate","license plate","lpr","recognition","fail","失敗","車牌","識別","柵欄","閘桿","privacy","私隱","secure element","安全元件","cost","成本","low cost","低成本"],"category":"overview","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"products","title":"Metre products: MetreTag, MetrePoint, Metre App and Console","text":"MetreTag is the UWB device installed inside the vehicle (usually on the windscreen). It is powered by a standard 5V supply, like a dashcam, and works independently of the phone. MetrePoint is the UWB reader installed at the car-park entrance / exit that recognises the tag and lifts the barrier automatically. The Metre App lets drivers see real-time parking status, transparent pricing, detailed records, whitelist their vehicle with a Metre ID, and pay with FPS. The Metre Console (console.metre.hk) is the online management service for car-park operators (merchants): it shows device health, car-park status, access lists, today's revenue, total traffic and transaction history, and supports settlement / CSV export.","keywords":["metretag","metrepoint","metre app","console","tag","reader","barrier","app","管理","控制台","dashboard","settlements","devices","transaction"],"category":"products","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"features","title":"Key features and benefits","text":"Key features: (1) UWB contactless entry and exit — the barrier rises automatically; (2) Centimetre-level spatial algorithms prevent accidental triggers from cars passing nearby; (3) Privacy — whitelist with a Metre ID, no licence plate required, end-to-end encryption, location records used only for billing; (4) Tamper-resistant payments — IEEE 802.15.4z Scrambled Timestamp Sequence (STS) prevents signal-energy injection and spoofing; (5) Lost mode — if the phone is lost, the tag can be protected immediately from the app; (6) Low cost — the e-ID is stored on the phone's secure element, no expensive on-site hardware upgrades; (7) FPS payment in the app, with a HK$100 seamless-exit buffer; (8) Use cases: access control, self-service kiosks, school attendance and parking.","keywords":["feature","功能","uwb","contactless","無感","privacy","私隱","sts","ieee 802.15.4z","lost mode","遺失","low cost","低成本","fps","轉數快","buffer","額度","use case","應用","access control","門禁","attendance","考勤","parking","泊車"],"category":"features","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"home-zh","title":"Metre 車主頁 (zh-hant-hk)","text":"﻿\n車主 | 一米通\n車主\n商戶\nEnglish\n繁體·香港\n繁體·台灣\n简体中文\nMetreTag\n車主無感出入閘\n駛近 MetrePoint，閘桿將自動升起，無需操作\n立即出 Tag\n查看 MetreTag 安裝指南\n搜尋 MetrePoint\n搜尋\n中環\n尖沙咀\n灣仔\n觀塘\n旺角\n停車場\n區域\n分區\n類別\n地址\n搵唔到相關停車場，請試其他關鍵字。\n搜尋中…\n← 返回搜尋結果\n超寬頻 (UWB)\n不止快狠準\n保障你的私隱\n添加白名單只需提供 Metre ID，無需車牌。\n全方位掌握泊車動態\n透過一米通 App，所有泊車資訊一目了然：\n即時狀態\n隨時查看已泊時間及累積泊車費用。\n收費透明\n清晰列明各停車場的收費計算規則。\n詳細紀錄\n完整保存過往的泊車與付款紀錄，方便查閱。\n隨時隨地 App 內以 FPS 付費\n無感出閘付款僅有 HK$100 額度。\n累計多於 HK$100 需出閘前或出閘時付款。\n無論如何，你都可以先核實，後付款。\n所有未繳費用必須於 7 天內完成支付。\n立即下載 App 以 HK$100 按金出 Tag\n*MetreTag 之按金與此限額無關，且不作任何付款用途。\n常見問題\n如何退還按金？\n當你退還 MetreTag 時，工程師會檢查是否存在惡意破壞情況。如無，按金將沿原路退回。\nMetreTag 如何避免盜刷？\nMetreTag 使用超寬頻作為付款依據，其所採用的 IEEE 802.15.4z 標準中引入的一個關鍵特性為加擾時間戳序列（STS）。透過 STS 安全機制，可以防止惡意裝置透過注入訊號能量進行不同形式的攻擊，從而確保付款真實性。\nMetreTag 是否準確？\n超寬頻帶來的厘米級空間算法，避免了在附近駛過誤觸的尷尬情況。\nMetreTag 如何供電？\n與一般車 cam 一樣，以 5 伏供電即可。\n如果我的手機沒電了，還能自動扣款嗎？\n可以。MetreTag 是獨立運作的硬件裝置，只要裝置安裝在車內，即使手機無電或不在身邊，MetrePoint 仍能識別 MetreTag 並自動完成扣款。\n我的行蹤數據會被外洩嗎？\n絕對不會。我們採用最高規格的端到端加密技術，你的進出紀錄僅用於計費用途。我們不會收集、追蹤或向任何第三方出售你的位置數據。\n支援哪些付款方式？\n目前只支援 FPS 付款方式。期後將會支援其他自動扣款方式，敬請期待。\nCopyright ©\n一米通有限公司 保留一切權利。\n私隱政策\n|\n使用條款\n|\n聯絡我們\n香港\n-->\nEnglish\n繁體中文（香港）\n繁體中文（台灣）\n简体中文","keywords":["車主","首頁","metretag","metrepoint","泊車","fps","轉數快","按金","deposit"],"category":"home","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"home-en","title":"Metre driver home page (en)","text":"﻿\nDriver | Metre\nDriver\nBusiness\nEnglish\n繁體·香港\n繁體·台灣\n简体中文\nMetreTag\nAlways Reliable\nDrive near the MetrePoint and the barrier rises automatically\nNo action required\nGet Tag\nView MetreTag Installation Guide\nSearch MetrePoint\nSearch\nCentral\nTsim Sha Tsui\nWan Chai\nKwun Tong\nMong Kok\nCar Park\nRegion\nDistrict\nCategory\nAddress\nNo matching car parks found. Try another keyword.\nSearching…\n← Back to results\nULTRA-WIDEBAND (UWB)\nBeyond Speed and Precision\nProtect Your Privacy\nWhitelist your vehicle using only your Metre ID.\nNo licence plate required.\nComprehensive Parking Dashboard\nWith the Metre app, all your parking information is clear at a glance:\nReal-time Status\nCheck your parked duration and accumulated fees anytime.\nTransparent Pricing\nClear breakdown of pricing rules for every car park.\nDetailed Records\nComplete history of your parking and payment records for easy access.\nPay via FPS Anywhere, Anytime in the App\nSeamless auto-payment is limited to HK$100.\nAccumulated fees over HK$100 must be paid before or upon exiting.\nEither way, you can always verify the amount before paying.\nAll outstanding fees must be paid within 7 days.\nDownload the App & Get Your Tag with a HK$100 Deposit\n*The MetreTag deposit is unrelated to this limit and cannot be used for payments.\nFrequently Asked Questions\nHow do I get my deposit refunded?\nWhen you return your MetreTag, an engineer checks it for deliberate damage. If there is none, the deposit is refunded to your original payment method.\nHow does MetreTag prevent unauthorised scanning?\nMetreTag settles payments over Ultra-Wideband. The IEEE 802.15.4z standard it uses introduces the Scrambled Timestamp Sequence (STS), a security mechanism that stops malicious devices from injecting signal energy to spoof distance, so every payment stays authentic.\nIs MetreTag accurate?\nCentimetre-level spatial algorithms from UWB prevent accidental triggers when you simply drive past.\nHow is MetreTag powered?\nIt runs on a standard 5V supply, just like a typical dashcam.\nIf my phone battery dies, will automatic payment still work?\nYes. MetreTag is an independent hardware device. As long as it is installed in your car, MetrePoint recognises it and completes payment automatically, even if your phone is dead or not with you.\nWill my location data be leaked?\nNo. We use end-to-end encryption, and your entry and exit records are used strictly for billing. We never collect, track, or sell your location data to third parties.\nWhat payment methods are supported?\nFPS only for now. More automatic payment methods are on the way.\nCopyright ©\nMetre Ltd. All rights reserved.\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nTerms of Use\n|\nContact\nHong Kong\n-->\nEnglish\n繁體中文（香港）\n繁體中文（台灣）\n简体中文","keywords":["driver","home","metretag","metrepoint","parking","fps","deposit"],"category":"home","lang":"en"},{"id":"business-zh","title":"Metre 商戶頁 — 定價方案 (zh-hant-hk)","text":"MetrePoint 全港獨家 UWB 技術，無感通行連支付整合，免升級費、免費對接現有閘機，首 3 個月免費試用。買斷方案：HK$30,000 每部，包含 UWB 門禁管理及無感支付、基本安裝服務、首年系統對接服務、首年技術支援及保修；網上管理服務需額外付費；付款手續費 2.0%。月租方案：每部 HK$38/月，每月交易額每滿 HK$50,000 豁免一部已啟用 MetrePoint 的月費；包含首 3 個月免費試用、UWB 門禁管理及無感支付、標準安裝服務、系統對接與升級服務、技術支援及維護、非人為硬件損壞免費保修更換、網上管理服務；付款手續費 1.5%，最快 T+1 到帳。申請請往 console.metre.hk 或 WhatsApp 85259117372。","keywords":["商戶","business","定價","ricing","買斷","月租","hk$30,000","hk$38","手續費","2.0%","1.5%","t+1","metrepoint","uwb","閘機","免費試用","free trial"],"category":"business","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"business-en","title":"Metre business page — pricing (en)","text":"MetrePoint: exclusive UWB technology in Hong Kong, seamless access control with payment integration, no upgrade fee and free integration with existing gates, first 3 months free trial. One-time buyout: HK$30,000 each, including UWB access control and payment, basic installation, first-year system integration, first-year tech support and warranty; online management service is charged separately; payment handling fee 2.0%. Monthly subscription: HK$38 per unit per month; for every HK$50,000 of monthly transaction volume, the monthly fee for one deployed MetrePoint is waived. It includes a 3-month free trial, UWB access control and payment, standard installation, system integration and upgrades, technical support and maintenance, free warranty replacement for non-human hardware damage, and online management service; payment handling fee 1.5%, settlement as fast as T+1. Apply at console.metre.hk or WhatsApp 85259117372.","keywords":["business","pricing","buyout","monthly","hk$30,000","hk$38","handling fee","2.0%","1.5%","t+1","metrepoint","uwb","free trial"],"category":"business","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-zh-1","title":"如何退還按金？","text":"問：如何退還按金？\n答：當你退還 MetreTag 時，工程師會檢查是否存在惡意破壞情況。如無，按金將沿原路退回。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-zh-2","title":"MetreTag 如何避免盜刷？","text":"問：MetreTag 如何避免盜刷？\n答：MetreTag 使用超寬頻作為付款依據，其所採用的 IEEE 802.15.4z 標準中引入的一個關鍵特性為加擾時間戳序列（STS）。透過 STS 安全機制，可以防止惡意裝置透過注入訊號能量進行不同形式的攻擊，從而確保付款真實性。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-zh-3","title":"MetreTag 是否準確？","text":"問：MetreTag 是否準確？\n答：超寬頻帶來的厘米級空間算法，避免了在附近駛過誤觸的尷尬情況。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-zh-4","title":"MetreTag 如何供電？","text":"問：MetreTag 如何供電？\n答：與一般車 cam 一樣，以 5 伏供電即可。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-zh-5","title":"如果我的手機沒電了，還能自動扣款嗎？","text":"問：如果我的手機沒電了，還能自動扣款嗎？\n答：可以。MetreTag 是獨立運作的硬件裝置，只要裝置安裝在車內，即使手機無電或不在身邊，MetrePoint 仍能識別 MetreTag 並自動完成扣款。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-zh-6","title":"我的行蹤數據會被外洩嗎？","text":"問：我的行蹤數據會被外洩嗎？\n答：絕對不會。我們採用最高規格的端到端加密技術，你的進出紀錄僅用於計費用途。我們不會收集、追蹤或向任何第三方出售你的位置數據。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-zh-7","title":"支援哪些付款方式？","text":"問：支援哪些付款方式？\n答：目前只支援 FPS 付款方式。期後將會支援其他自動扣款方式，敬請期待。","keywords":["常見問題","faq","按金","deposit","盜刷","sts","準確","供電","手機","行蹤","私隱","付款","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"faq-en-1","title":"How do I get my deposit refunded?","text":"Q: How do I get my deposit refunded?\nA: When you return your MetreTag, an engineer checks it for deliberate damage. If there is none, the deposit is refunded to your original payment method.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-en-2","title":"How does MetreTag prevent unauthorised scanning?","text":"Q: How does MetreTag prevent unauthorised scanning?\nA: MetreTag settles payments over Ultra-Wideband. The IEEE 802.15.4z standard it uses introduces the Scrambled Timestamp Sequence (STS), a security mechanism that stops malicious devices from injecting signal energy to spoof distance, so every payment stays authentic.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-en-3","title":"Is MetreTag accurate?","text":"Q: Is MetreTag accurate?\nA: Centimetre-level spatial algorithms from UWB prevent accidental triggers when you simply drive past.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-en-4","title":"How is MetreTag powered?","text":"Q: How is MetreTag powered?\nA: It runs on a standard 5V supply, just like a typical dashcam.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-en-5","title":"If my phone battery dies, will automatic payment still work?","text":"Q: If my phone battery dies, will automatic payment still work?\nA: Yes. MetreTag is an independent hardware device. As long as it is installed in your car, MetrePoint recognises it and completes payment automatically, even if your phone is dead or not with you.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-en-6","title":"Will my location data be leaked?","text":"Q: Will my location data be leaked?\nA: No. We use end-to-end encryption, and your entry and exit records are used strictly for billing. We never collect, track, or sell your location data to third parties.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"faq-en-7","title":"What payment methods are supported?","text":"Q: What payment methods are supported?\nA: FPS only for now. More automatic payment methods are on the way.","keywords":["faq","deposit","refund","unauthorised","sts","accurate","powered","phone","battery","location","privacy","payment","fps"],"category":"faq","lang":"en"},{"id":"installation-guide","title":"MetreTag 安裝指南 (Installation Guide)","text":"--- page 1 ---\nMetreTag 安裝指南 \n \n選購配件（如有需要） \n在安裝 MetreTag 前，請先確認您行車記錄儀的電源線接口類型，並依據下列指示在「一米通 \nApp」選購或向管理處領取相應配件： \n• 如果您行車記錄器的電源線接口為 Type-C，請選購 Type-C 車 Cam 用一分二。 \n \n• 如果您行車記錄器的電源線接口為 Micro USB，請選購 Micro USB 車 Cam 用一分二。 \n \n• 如果 MetreTag 安裝空間不足，或日後需要調整 MetreTag 的擺放位置，建議一併選購延長\n線。由於我們於 MetreTag 寄出時已隨附黏貼貼紙，您可以放心地將 MetreTag 黏貼於車窗\n上的合適位置，無需擔心固定問題。 \n \n\n--- page 2 ---\n重要提示 \n您必須僅使用我們直接提供、或透過 Metre App 訂購的電源線、延長線及變壓器。 \n使用任何未經授權的第三方線材、經改裝的線路，或非經核准的電源變壓器，均屬不當使用；因此而導\n致的任何硬件損壞或故障，將由您自行承擔全部責任。 \n \nMetreTag 安裝位置 \n請將 MetreTag 安裝於擋風玻璃之中上位置附近，如下圖所示： \n \n安裝步驟： \n1. 清潔擋風玻璃之中上位置，確保表面乾淨、乾燥、無油污。 \n2. 撕開 MetreTag 背面貼紙的保護膜。 \n3. 將 MetreTag 平整地黏貼於擋風玻璃之中上位置。 \n4. 接駁電源線，並確認 MetreTag 的聲音顯示正常運作。 \n \n\n--- page 3 ---\n或輕易地將 MetreTag 接駁車 Cam 用一分二，如下圖所示： \n \n重要提示 \n您必須嚴格按照我們的指示及指引，安裝、固定、供電及操作您的 MetreTag。 \n請勿將多個信號發射裝置、金屬遮擋物或其他射頻（RF）干擾裝置，放置於 MetreTag 附近，以免影響\n感應偵測及閘口通訊，任何因此產生的干擾風險由您自行承擔。 \n對於因安裝不當、使用未經授權的電源配件，或外部信號干擾而導致的停車記錄遺漏或錯誤記錄、閘口\n延誤或硬件故障，我們概不負責。 \n聯絡我們 \n如您於安裝過程中遇到任何問題，歡迎透過以下方式與我們聯絡： \n• 電郵：support@metre.hk \n• 電話：5911 7372 \n• 網站：www.metre.hk \n• 辦公時間：星期一至六，上午 9 時至下午 9 時，星期日及公眾假期休息。","keywords":["安裝","install","guide","指引","metretag","擋風玻璃","windscreen","電源線","type-c","micro usb","車 cam","一分二","延長線","support","聯絡"],"category":"installation","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"fees-schedule","title":"Schedule of Fees and Guidelines (服務收費及指引)","text":"--- page 1 ---\nSchedule of Fees and Guidelines \nEffective from 7 August 2026 \nThis Schedule supplements the Conditions of Issue issued by METRE HONG KONG \nLIMITED (\"Metre\", \"we\", or \"us\"). This Schedule is effective from 7 August 2026 until such \ntime as an updated version is issued. \n1. General Enquiries and Support \nIf you have any enquiries regarding your On-Loan MetreTag, session records, or account \nstatus, or if you need to report a lost or stolen MetreTag, please contact us via WhatsApp at \n(852) 5911 7372 or email us at support@metre.hk. \n2. Fee Structure and Operational Charges \nFee Amount Condition reference \n(a) MetreTag Deposit HK$100 Conditions 5.1–5.3 \n(b) Delivery Fee HK$20 Conditions 4.2, 10.1(c) \n(c) Redelivery Fee HK$20 Condition 4.3 \n(d) Physical Damage Fee HK$50 Conditions 7.1, 10.1(b) \n(e) Reactivation Fee HK$10 Conditions 10.3(b), 11.3 \n(f) Late Payment / Buffer Administrative \nCharge \nHK$20 Condition 6.5 \n3. Governing Language \nIf there is any inconsistency or discrepancy between the English version and any Chinese \ntranslation of this Schedule, the English version shall strictly prevail.","keywords":["fee","收費","deposit","按金","hk$100","delivery","運費","hk$20","damage","損壞","hk$50","reactivation","重新啟動","hk$10","late payment","逾期","buffer","行政費","support","whatsapp","5911 7372"],"category":"fees","lang":"en"},{"id":"terms-of-use-2","title":"Metre App Terms of Use (條款及細則) part 2","text":"Metre App Terms of Use \nPlease read these Terms of Use (\"Terms of Use\") carefully. By downloading, accessing, \nor using this mobile application (\"Metre App\") operated by METRE HONG KONG LIMITED \n(\"Metre\" , \"we\" , or \"us\") and accessing the content, information, and services available \nthrough the Metre App, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Use. These Terms of \nUse are to be read together with the Conditions of Issue of MetreTag published by Metre \n(as amended from time to time) and posted on our official website at www.metre.hk. \nMetre reserves the right to amend these Terms of Use at any time by publishing updated \nterms within the Metre App or on our website. Your continued use of the Metre App \nfollowing any such amendments constitutes your agreement to be bound by the \nupdated Terms of Use. \nUser Eligibility and Account Registration \nTo access certain features of the Metre App, you may be required to register for an \naccount. When registering, you agree to provide accurate, current, and complete \ninformation as prompted, and to promptly update such information to keep it accurate, \ncurrent, and complete. You are solely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of \nyour account credentials and for all activities that occur under your account. You agree \nto notify Metre immediately of any unauthorized use of your account or any other \nbreach of security. Metre shall not be liable for any loss or damage arising from your \nfailure to comply with these obligations. \nProprietary Content \nThe content, software, interface designs, information, and materials contained in or \nrendered by the Metre App are proprietary in nature and are owned by Metre. \nIntellectual Property Rights \nThe trademarks, logos, copyrights, software code, UI design, patents, and all other \nintellectual property rights in the content, features, or materials available on or through \nthe Metre App are owned by Metre or its licensors. No part of the content, code, or \ninformation available on or through the Metre App may be modified, reverse-\nengineered, reproduced, stored in a retrieval system, transmitted, copied, distributed, \nor used in any other way without the prior written consent of Metre or the relevant \nintellectual property owner. \nNo Warranties and Limitation of Liability","keywords":["terms","條款","使用條款","account","帳戶","proprietary"," intellectual","warranty","擔保","liability","責任","device data","資料","governing law","香港","jurisdiction"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"terms-of-use-3","title":"Metre App Terms of Use (條款及細則) part 3","text":"The Metre App and all content, software functions, and services provided through it are \noffered on an \"as is\" and \"as available\" basis. Metre makes no express or implied \nwarranties, representations, or endorsements whatsoever regarding the Metre App, its \ncompatibility with your mobile device, or the continuity of its services. Metre does not \nwarrant that the Metre App will be uninterrupted, error-free, or completely free of \nsoftware bugs or security vulnerabilities. You are solely responsible for providing \nadequate security and backup for your mobile device and data. Metre makes no \nwarranty regarding the reliability, functionality, availability, accuracy, or fitness for a \nparticular purpose of the Metre App or its real-time parking access and billing features. \nTo the maximum extent permitted by Hong Kong law, in no event shall Metre or its \naffiliates be held liable for any claim, loss, damage, costs, or expenses (whether direct, \nindirect, special, or consequential) arising out of or in connection with the downloading, \ninstallation, or use of the Metre App, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), or \notherwise, even if Metre has been advised of the possibility of such damages. Nothing in \nthese Terms shall exclude or limit any liability that cannot be excluded or limited under \napplicable Hong Kong law. \nProvision of Information and Device Data \nDepending on the service requested, Metre may require you to provide information that \nenables us to manage your account and deliver services, such as your email address, \nOn-Loan MetreTag ID, mobile device identifiers (identifierForVendor / Android ID), push \nnotification tokens, and parking session location logs. For full details on how we collect, \nuse, retain, and protect your personal data, please refer to our Personal Information \nCollection Statement (PICS) and Privacy Policy Statement, accessible in the Metre App \nsettings and at www.metre.hk. \nExternal Links and Third-Party Portals \nThe Metre App may provide links or deep-links to external websites or third-party \nservices (such as mobile banking or FPS payment interfaces). When navigating away \nfrom the Metre App to external platforms, you are subject to the privacy policies and \nterms of use of those respective third-party providers. \nUpdates to the Service \nThe features, user interfaces, and functionality of the Metre App describe our current \npractice. Metre reserves the right to modify, update, add, or discontinue features of the \nMetre App at any time without prior notice. \nGoverning Language \nThese Terms of Use may be translated into Chinese for reference purposes. If there is \nany inconsistency or discrepancy between the English version and any Chinese \ntranslation, the English version shall prevail.","keywords":["terms","條款","使用條款","account","帳戶","proprietary"," intellectual","warranty","擔保","liability","責任","device data","資料","governing law","香港","jurisdiction"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"terms-of-use-4","title":"Metre App Terms of Use (條款及細則) part 4","text":"Governing Law and Jurisdiction \nThese Terms of Use shall be governed by, and construed in accordance with, the laws of \nthe Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. You and Metre irrevocably agree that the \ncourts of Hong Kong shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim \narising out of or in connection with these Terms of Use. \nRights of Third Parties \nNo person other than you and METRE HONG KONG LIMITED shall have any right to \nenforce or rely on any provision of these Terms of Use under the Contracts (Rights of \nThird Parties) Ordinance (Cap. 623) or otherwise.","keywords":["terms","條款","使用條款","account","帳戶","proprietary"," intellectual","warranty","擔保","liability","責任","device data","資料","governing law","香港","jurisdiction"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-1","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 1","text":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag \n(Effective from 9 Aug 2026) \n \nYOUR ATTENTION IS DRAWN TO CONDITION 10 AND THE PERSONAL INFORMATION \nCOLLECTION STATEMENT IN CONDITION 13\n1. Conditions of Issue \nThese Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (these \"Conditions of Issue\") are effective from 9 \nAug 2026 for all customers.\n2. Introduction \n2.1. These Conditions of Issue constitute a legally binding contract between you (our \ncustomer) and us, METRE HONG KONG LIMITED (the issuer of the MetreTag and \noperator of the Metre App). By ordering, activating, or using a MetreTag, or by using the \nMetre App, you agree to be fully bound by these Conditions of Issue. \n2.2. These Conditions of Issue set out our mutual rights and obligations. While they \ngovern the general use of the MetreTag and the Metre App, they may be complemented, \nsupplemented, or modified by specific terms and conditions applicable to particular \nfeatures or services that we may offer from time to time. \n2.3. There are key terms used in these Conditions of Issue which are defined as follows: \n(a) \"Schedule of Fees and Guidelines\" means the schedule of fees, deposits, \nadministrative charges, and guidelines published by us, Metre Hong Kong Limited, as \namended from time to time. The latest version can be accessed via the Metre App or on \nour official website at www.metre.hk. \n(b) \"Service Provider\" means any car park operator, property manager, access control \noperator, or mobility service provider that utilizes the Metre system to record parking \nsessions, grant vehicle access, or manage parking premises, and has been approved by \nus. Service Providers will clearly display the Metre acceptance logo at their physical \nlocations, access barriers, or within online channels.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-2","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 2","text":"3. General \n3.1. \"On-Loan MetreTag\" is a MetreTag which we lend to you and which we will require \nyou to pay a Deposit. Subject to Condition 10.2, you may return your On-Loan MetreTag \nfor a refund. \n3.2. We operate the Metre system and will ensure that the system is operated with \nreasonable care, skill, and diligence. The MetreTag functions to record your parking \nsessions. If you discover any discrepancies regarding your recorded parking sessions or \n\nparking fees in the Metre App, you should contact us (see Condition 20) as soon as \npossible. \n3.3. The MetreTag enables participating Service Providers displaying the Metre \nacceptance logo to automatically record your entry, exit, and parking session duration. \nYou agree to settle all incurred parking fees resulting from recorded sessions through \nthe Metre App, subject to any transaction rules or limits we may notify you of from time \nto time. \n3.4. Some Service Providers may use your MetreTag strictly for premises access control \nwithout immediately concluding or displaying a completed parking session. \n3.5. A Service Provider can be identified by their clear display of the Metre acceptance \nlogo, whether online, at physical locations, or otherwise. Please contact the Service \nProvider or us if a Service Provider fails to recognize your MetreTag for session recording. \n3.6. Service Providers are responsible for all aspects of the physical parking facilities \nand services they provide. In using their services and facilities, you should abide by their \nrules, regulations, and bylaws. We have no responsibility for the physical facilities or \nparking services provided by Service Providers, and you should direct any enquiries \nrelating to facility condition or management to the relevant Service Provider. \n3.7. Under normal circumstances, we will make reasonable efforts to ensure that the \nMetre system is operating. However, we cannot guarantee that a Service Provider's \nhardware will successfully scan or record a MetreTag session at all times, as this \ndepends on the Service Provider's own systems, as well as network, electrical, climatic, \nand other conditions beyond our control. Subject to Condition 8.4, we shall not be \nresponsible for any indirect, consequential, or special loss or damage incurred by you \nas a result of or in connection with your use of the MetreTag or the Metre App, including \nbut not limited to loss of profit, loss of revenue, loss of business, or loss of anticipated \nsavings. For the avoidance of doubt, nothing in these Conditions of Issue shall exclude \nor restrict our liability for direct loss or damage caused by our wilful default or gross \nnegligence. \n3.8. We may charge a reasonable fee for the provision of the MetreTag, Metre App, and \nrelated services. Any such fees will be published in our Schedule of Fees and \nGuidelines. \n3.9. If any provision of these Conditions of Issue is held to be invalid, illegal, or \nunenforceable by any court of competent jurisdiction, such provision shall be severed \nfrom these Conditions of Issue to the extent of such invalidity, illegality, or \nunenforceability, and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect. \n3.10. These Conditions of Issue, together with any supplemental terms and conditions \nissued pursuant to Condition 2.2, constitute the entire agreement between you and us \n\nwith respect to the use of the MetreTag and the Metre App, and supersede all prior or \ncontemporaneous representations, understandings, or agreements, whether written or \noral, relating to the subject matter hereof. \n3.11. No failure or delay by us in exercising any right, power, or remedy under these \nConditions of Issue shall operate as a waiver of that right, power, or remedy, nor shall \nany single or partial exercise of any such right, power, or remedy preclude any other or \nfurther exercise thereof or the exercise of any other right, power, or remedy.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-3","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 3","text":"4. Obtaining and Using your MetreTag; Registering for the Metre App \n4.1. You must be at least 18 years of age to order a MetreTag, create a Metre App \naccount, or use the Metre service. By ordering a MetreTag or registering for the Metre \nApp, you represent and warrant that you are at least 18 years old and have the legal \ncapacity to enter into these Conditions of Issue. \n4.2. To use the Metre service, you must order an On-Loan MetreTag directly through the \nMetre App. Upon completion of your order and payment of any required Deposit and \ndelivery fee, we will dispatch and deliver the MetreTag to your designated shipping \naddress. By activating or using the MetreTag, you agree to be bound by these Conditions \nof Issue. \n4.3. Delivery, Risk of Loss, and Non-Delivery \n(a) Risk and Delivery: Risk of loss or damage to the On-Loan MetreTag shall pass to you \nonly upon successful physical delivery to your designated address or upon sign-\noff/acknowledgment of receipt from the designated courier or postal service. \n(b) Transit Damage or Loss in Transit: If the MetreTag is lost, delayed, or physically \ndamaged during transit prior to successful delivery, we will, upon prompt notification \nand verification, arrange a replacement MetreTag to be dispatched to you free of charge. \nWe shall handle all claims, inquiries, and compensation disputes directly with the \nrelevant courier or postal service provider. \n(c) Failed Delivery and Loss Due to User Error: \n(i) Returned Shipments: If a MetreTag is returned to us intact due to an \nincorrect/incomplete address or failure to collect, you will be required to pay the \nRedelivery Fee (as set out in the Schedule of Fees and Guidelines) prior to re-delivery. \n(ii) Lost Shipments: If a MetreTag is permanently lost or unrecoverable as a direct result \nof an incorrect address or invalid delivery information provided by you, the MetreTag \nshall be deemed lost. We reserve the right to forfeit your Deposit to cover the cost of the \nlost hardware. To receive a new MetreTag, you will be required to submit a new order and \ndeposit via the Metre App. \n\n4.4. The MetreTag is non-transferable. You must not sell, lend, or transfer your MetreTag \nto any third party without our prior written consent. The registered holder of the Metre \nApp account associated with the MetreTag will remain solely responsible for all parking \nsessions and fees recorded by that MetreTag. \n4.5. All On-Loan MetreTags remain our physical property at all times. We retain the right \nto manage, update, or deactivate the software, firmware, and data loaded on your \nMetreTag, as well as the right to recall or recover the MetreTag, at our sole discretion. \n4.6. A \"valid MetreTag\" means a genuine MetreTag: \n(a) which has been lawfully obtained directly from us via the Metre App; \n(b) which is successfully bound to an active Metre App account; and \n(c) which has not been damaged, tampered with, altered, or physically compromised. \n4.7. To access parking services and settle incurred parking fees, you must maintain a \nvalid registration. \n4.8. If you suspect that your MetreTag or Metre App account has been lost, stolen, or \nused for unauthorized parking sessions, you must immediately report it to us through \nthe Metre App or via our customer support (see Condition 20). \n4.9. Upon receiving notification of a lost, stolen, or compromised MetreTag, we will \ndeactivate the MetreTag as soon as reasonably practicable. You will remain responsible \nfor all parking fees incurred and recorded by the MetreTag prior to the completion of the \ndeactivation process. \n4.10. To protect your account security, we may perform additional user authentication \nprocedures within the Metre App before processing high-value transactions or adjusting \ncritical account settings.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-4","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 4","text":"5. Paying a Deposit for Your On-Loan MetreTag \n5.1. When you order an On-Loan MetreTag through the Metre App, you will be required to \npay a security deposit (\"Deposit\") via your selected payment method in the Metre App \nprior to dispatch and delivery. \n5.2. We will hold the Deposit as security for the On-Loan MetreTag throughout the \nduration of your use of the Metre services. \n5.3. The amount of the Deposit shall be determined and announced by us in the Metre \nApp or our Schedule of Fees and Guidelines from time to time. The Deposit serves to \ncover potential loss, hardware damage, or non-return of the On-Loan MetreTag, as well \nas outstanding parking fees or administrative costs associated with your account, \nsubject to Condition 10.2.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-5","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 5","text":"6. Parking Fee Settlement and Credit Buffer \n6.1. All incurred parking fees and charges resulting from recorded parking sessions \nmust be paid manually by you within the Metre App using Faster Payment System (FPS) \nor other manual payment methods approved by us from time to time. \n6.2. Seamless Exit Buffer: To enable seamless barrier clearance, we grant you an \naccumulated unpaid parking fee buffer limit of up to HK$100 (or such other limit as we \nmay announce from time to time). \n6.3. As long as your total outstanding, unpaid parking fees do not exceed the HK$100 \nbuffer limit, you are permitted to exit participating parking facilities immediately upon \nsession completion without paying on the spot at the exit barrier. \n6.4. You are required to settle all outstanding parking fees via FPS in the Metre App in a \ntimely manner. If a new or ongoing parking session causes your total accumulated \nunpaid balance to equal or exceed HK$100, you will not be eligible for seamless exit, \nand your MetreTag access may be temporarily restricted until all pending balances are \nfully settled via FPS in the Metre App. \n6.5. We reserve the right to adjust, suspend, or revoke your buffer limit, or apply \nreasonable administrative late payment charges as published in our Schedule of Fees \nand Guidelines. Save where such adjustment, suspension, or revocation is triggered by \nyour non-payment, default, or breach of these Conditions of Issue, we will provide you \nwith at least 7 days' prior notice via the Metre App before any reduction or revocation of \nyour buffer limit takes effect.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-6","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 6","text":"7. Your Obligations in Using your MetreTag and the Metre App \n7.1. You must take good care of your On-Loan MetreTag and exercise reasonable \nsecurity precautions to prevent physical damage, loss, tampering, or unauthorized use. \nYou must also maintain the security of your Metre App account, including safeguarding \nyour account login credentials and email verification details. If an On-Loan MetreTag is \nreturned to us damaged or altered (including through bending, cutting, breaking, \nopening the casing, graffiti, or unauthorized attachments), we reserve the right to forfeit \nyour Deposit or charge a reasonable damage fee as set out in the Schedule of Fees and \nGuidelines. \n7.2. You must not use, or allow anyone else to use, your MetreTag or Metre App account \nfor any unlawful, fraudulent, or illegal purposes. \n7.3. You should only present or utilize your MetreTag at parking facilities clearly \ndisplaying the Metre acceptance logo. Attempting to use the MetreTag with \nunauthorized or incompatible reading equipment may result in hardware failure, for \nwhich we bear no responsibility. \n\n7.4. You must not tamper with, reverse-engineer, modify, or attempt to extract data or \nfirmware from the MetreTag (including hardware security elements, cryptographic keys, \nor BLE/UWB transceivers). You must not exploit or interfere with the Metre App or \ndisrupt other users, and specifically, you must not use automated systems, scripts, or \nbots to access or manipulate parking session records or FPS payment workflows. \nTampering with the MetreTag or its transmitted data may constitute a criminal offence \nunder the Crimes Ordinance (Cap. 200), including but not limited to section 161 thereof \n(Access to Computer with Criminal or Dishonest Intent). \n7.5. We reserve the right to recover all reasonable costs, expenses, legal fees, losses, \nand damages incurred by us as a result of you altering, interfering with, or allowing any \nthird party to alter or interfere with the hardware, software, or session data of your \nMetreTag or Metre App account. \n7.6. You agree to fully cooperate with us and, where applicable, law enforcement \nagencies in investigating lost, stolen, or tampered MetreTags, suspicious parking \ntransactions, or non-payment of accumulated parking balances exceeding the buffer \nlimit referred to in Condition 6.2. \n7.7. Our staff and authorized representatives of participating parking Service Providers \nshall have the right to inspect your MetreTag and verify its associated active session \ndata in the Metre App at any reasonable time within participating parking premises.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-7","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 7","text":"8. Proper Use of your MetreTag and the Metre App \n8.1. You must install, mount, power, and operate your MetreTag strictly in accordance \nwith our instructions and guidelines. You shall only use power cables, extension cables, \nand adapters supplied directly by us or ordered through the Metre App. The use of any \nunauthorized third-party cables, modified wiring, or non-approved power adapters \nconstitutes improper use, and any resulting hardware damage or failure shall be your \nsole responsibility. Furthermore, placing multiple signal-emitting transceivers, metallic \nobstructions, or other radio-frequency (RF) interfering devices in close proximity to the \nMetreTag may disrupt session detection and barrier communication. Any such \ninterference shall be at your own risk. We shall not be responsible for missed or \nincorrectly recorded parking sessions, gate delays, or hardware failure caused by \nimproper installation, unauthorized power accessories, or external signal interference. \n8.2. We shall not be responsible for any personal injury, vehicular damage, or property \nloss/damage resulting from your inappropriate, negligent, or unauthorized use of the \nMetreTag, the Metre App, or parking entry/exit barriers. \n8.3. You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold us harmless against all actions, \nproceedings, liabilities, claims, losses, damages, and reasonable costs and expenses \n(including reasonable legal fees) that we may incur or sustain arising out of or in \n\nconnection with any misuse, unauthorized modification, or illegal operation of your \nMetreTag or Metre App account by you or any third party using your device, provided that \nthis indemnity shall not apply to the extent that such third-party access was caused by \na security vulnerability in the Metre App or Metre system that was within our reasonable \ncontrol. \n8.4. Nothing in these Conditions of Issue shall exclude or restrict our liability for death \nor personal injury resulting from our negligence, or liability for fraud or fraudulent \nmisrepresentation.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-8","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 8","text":"9. Malfunction \nIf your On-Loan MetreTag malfunctions due to no fault of yours, and you have not \ndamaged, opened, or tampered with it in any way: \n(a) Reporting and Return: You should report the issue immediately through customer \nsupport in the Metre App (see Condition 20) and return the malfunctioning MetreTag to \nus in accordance with our return instructions. \n(b) Replacement or Refund: Upon receiving and verifying that the MetreTag has suffered \na hardware or firmware failure not caused by user misuse, physical damage, or \ntampering, we will, at your option: \n(i) Dispatch a replacement On-Loan MetreTag to your designated shipping address \nwithout charging an additional Deposit; or \n(ii) Cancel your MetreTag order and refund your Deposit in full to your designated bank \naccount via FPS, subject to Condition 10.2. \n(c) Outstanding Balances: A malfunctioning MetreTag does not relieve you of the \nobligation to settle any valid, recorded parking fees incurred prior to the malfunction. \nAny pending parking fees must be fully settled via FPS within the Metre App.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-9","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 9","text":"10. Inactive Accounts, Non-Payment, and Cancellation of MetreTag \n10.1. Customer-Initiated Return & Cancellation \n(a) You may cancel your Metre account and return your On-Loan MetreTag at any time by \ninitiating a return request in the Metre App and shipping the MetreTag back to our \ndesignated address at your own expense. \n(b) Upon our physical receipt and inspection of the returned On-Loan MetreTag—and \nprovided you have no outstanding, overdue parking balances—we will refund your \nDeposit in full (less any applicable hardware damage fees set out in the Schedule of \nFees and Guidelines) via FPS to your designated bank account. \n(c) Delivery charges paid when the MetreTag was originally shipped are strictly non-\nrefundable. \n\n10.2. Overdue Parking Fees Deemed Improper Use \n(a) All parking fees recorded by your MetreTag must be settled via the Metre App in a \ntimely manner (and immediately for sessions exceeding the HK$100 threshold). \n(b) Deemed Improper Use: Allowing any recorded parking fee or session balance to \nremain unpaid for more than 7 days following the session date shall be strictly deemed \nImproper Use and a material breach of these Conditions of Issue under Section 8. \n(c) In the event of such Improper Use, we reserve the right, without prior notice, to: \n(i) Immediately deactivate and invalidate your On-Loan MetreTag; \n(ii) Deny your vehicle entry or exit clearance across all participating parking facilities; \n(iii) Terminate your Metre App account; and \n(iv) Full forfeiture of your Deposit as liquidated damages for contractual breach. The \nparties acknowledge and agree that the Deposit represents a genuine pre-estimate of \nthe losses and costs that we would incur as a result of such breach, including but not \nlimited to administrative costs of account management, system resources consumed, \nhardware depreciation, and the costs of investigating, processing, and recovering \noutstanding parking balances. This forfeiture is without prejudice to our right to pursue \nlegal action or debt recovery for all outstanding parking balances and legal costs. \n10.3. Inactive MetreTags and Invalidation \n(a) Your On-Loan MetreTag is issued for active use. If a MetreTag records no parking \nsessions or app activity for a continuous period of 12 months, we may deem the \nMetreTag inactive and deactivate its wireless signals for system security. \n(b) You may apply to reactivate an inactive MetreTag via the Metre App, subject to \nidentity verification and a reasonable Reactivation Fee as set out in our Schedule of \nFees and Guidelines. \n(c) Failure to Return Inactive Tag: If a MetreTag remains inactive for more than 24 months \nand you fail to return it upon our request, the On-Loan MetreTag will be permanently \ncanceled, and your Deposit will be forfeited to cover the cost of the unreturned \nhardware. \n10.4. Permanent Deactivation & Non-Transferability \n(a) Once a MetreTag is canceled or invalidated due to non-payment, inactivity, or \nbreach, it cannot be reactivated or rebound to any Metre App account. \n(b) Invalidated MetreTags must be returned to us by post immediately upon request. \n10.5. Deceased Account Holders \n\nIn the event of an account holder's death, a legal personal representative may request \naccount closure and Deposit return by providing proof of death and legal capacity. \nProvided all historical parking sessions were fully settled prior to death, any remaining \nDeposit will be remitted to the deceased's estate via FPS.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-10","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 10","text":"11. Lost or Stolen MetreTag \n11.1. Immediate Reporting: If your On-Loan MetreTag is lost, stolen, or compromised, \nyou must immediately report it via the Metre App or contact Customer Support (see \nCondition 20) to freeze and disable the MetreTag. \n11.2. Liability for Incurred Sessions: You shall remain responsible for all parking \nsessions and fees recorded by your MetreTag up until the exact time your lost report is \nsuccessfully processed and confirmed in the Metre App (\"Deactivation Time\"). We shall \nnot be liable for any unauthorized parking fees incurred prior to the Deactivation Time. \n11.3. Recovery and Reactivation: If you locate or recover a MetreTag that was previously \nreported lost or stolen, you may apply to unfreeze and reactivate the device via the \nMetre App. Reactivation is subject to identity verification, backend security validation, \nand payment of a reasonable Reactivation Fee as set out in our Schedule of Fees and \nGuidelines. \n11.4. Deposit Forfeiture & Replacement: \n(a) If an On-Loan MetreTag is lost or stolen and cannot be physically returned to us, your \noriginal Deposit will be forfeited to cover the hardware replacement cost. \n(b) To continue using the Metre service, you must order a replacement MetreTag via the \nMetre App and pay a new Deposit.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-11","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 11","text":"12. Refunds and System Records \n12.1. No Interest: Any eligible refund of a Deposit paid to you under these Conditions of \nIssue will be remitted without interest. \n12.2. Refund Processing via FPS: All authorized refunds (such as returned Deposit \nbalances upon account closure) will be remitted to your designated FPS bank account. \nIf a refund cannot be successfully transferred due to invalid user-provided account \ndetails and remains uncollected for 12 months despite reasonable notice, the refund \nclaim shall lapse, and the funds will be forfeited. \n12.3. System Records as Evidence: In determining whether a parking session occurred, \nthe duration of a parking session, or the status of a MetreTag, our server logs and system \ntransaction records shall serve as prima facie evidence, save in the case of manifest \ntechnical or system error on our part. \n\n12.4. Discharge of Liability: Upon your receipt and acceptance of any Deposit refund, \nyou agree to discharge us from any further claims or liabilities relating to the returned \nOn-Loan MetreTag or associated Metre App account.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-12","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 12","text":"13. Personal Information Collection Statement (PICS) in accordance with the \nPersonal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (Cap. 486) \n13.1. General \nThe Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (the \"Ordinance\") governs the collection, \nholding, processing, and use of your personal data and other information that we may \ncollect from time to time (\"Data\"). The Data shall include your account profile details, \ndelivery address, app usage records, and transactional/session records (meaning \nparking entry/exit timestamps, location logs, and billing history) to the extent that such \nrecords constitute personal data under the Ordinance. This Notice forms the basis \nupon which we collect, hold, process, and use your Data to provide the MetreTag, Metre \nApp, and related parking settlement services to you. \n13.2. Obligation to Provide Data \nIt is voluntary for you to provide your Data. However, if you choose not to provide the \nrequested Data, we may be unable to process your MetreTag order, deliver the On-Loan \nMetreTag to your address, bind your MetreTag to your Metre App account, or provide \nparking access and transaction services to you. \n13.3. Direct Marketing \nWe intend to use your Data to send you direct marketing communications regarding our \nproducts, services, special promotions, and offers relating to parking and mobility \nservices. \n(a) Data Used: Your email address, and/or device identification tokens (for push \nnotifications). (Note: We do not collect or use your phone number for marketing or \naccount creation). \n(b) Channels: In-app push notifications and email. \n(c) Consent & Opt-Out: We will not use your Data for direct marketing without your \nexplicit consent. You may exercise your right to opt-out of direct marketing at any time, \nfree of charge, directly within the Metre App settings or by contacting our Data \nProtection Officer. \n13.4. Purpose of Collection \nYou agree that your Data may be collected, held, and used by us for the following \npurposes: \n\n(a) Processing your application for an On-Loan MetreTag, verifying your identity, and \nshipping the MetreTag to your designated delivery address; \n(b) Managing, operating, maintaining, and improving the Metre App, MetreTag wireless \nsession logs, and post-session billing/FPS settlement systems; \n(c) Communicating with you regarding your account, transaction alerts, system \nupdates, and customer support inquiries; \n(d) Investigating complaints, disputed parking session records, system malfunctions, or \nsuspected fraudulent activity/unauthorized tag usage; \n(e) Collecting outstanding parking balances or debt recovery in the event of default or \ncontractual breach; \n(f) Designing new mobility services or enhancing existing features provided by us and \nour affiliates; and \n(g) Complying with applicable laws, regulations, legal proceedings, or enforceable \ngovernmental/regulatory requests in Hong Kong. \n13.5. Transfer and Disclosure of Data \nYour Data will be kept confidential by us. However, for the purposes set out in Condition \n13.4, we may transfer or disclose your Data to the following parties (who owe a duty of \nconfidentiality to us): \n(a) Service Providers & Contractors: Third-party vendors who provide administrative, \ncourier/logistics (for MetreTag shipping), cloud server hosting, data processing, FPS \npayment gateway execution, debt collection, or IT support services in connection with \nour operations; \n(b) Parking Operators: Participating car park owners and operators displaying the Metre \nacceptance logo, solely to the extent necessary to verify premises entry/exit, clear \nbarrier gates, or resolve session timing discrepancies; \n(c) Affiliates: Our subsidiaries and direct holding company for internal operations and \nservice administration; and \n(d) Legal & Regulatory Authorities: Law enforcement agencies, courts, or regulatory \nbodies in Hong Kong where we are legally required to satisfy a binding disclosure \ndemand or court order. \nWe will strictly not sell, rent, or transfer your personal data to third parties for their own \ndirect marketing purposes. \n13.6. Your Rights (Access and Correction) \nUnder the Ordinance, you have the right to: \n\n(a) Check whether we hold Data about you and request access to such Data; \n(b) Request us to correct any inaccurate Data relating to you; \n(c) Ascertain our privacy policies and practices regarding personal data; and \n(d) Request that we cease using your Data for direct marketing purposes at any time \nwithout charge. \n13.7. Data Access Requests \nWe reserve the right to charge a reasonable fee for processing any physical Data Access \nRequest under the Ordinance. Any request for access to or correction of Data, or for \ninformation regarding our privacy practices, should be submitted in writing to: \nData Protection Officer METRE HONG KONG LIMITED \nFlat 1229, Kai Fai House, Choi Wan (II) Estate, Kowloon, Hong Kong \nEmail: privacy@metre.hk","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-13","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 13","text":"14. Session and Transaction Records \n14.1. Access to Session History \n(a) You may view your recent parking session records and transaction history directly \nwithin the Metre App at any time without additional charge. \n(b) Transaction records available in the Metre App include entry and exit timestamps, \nparking duration, participating car park locations, and corresponding parking fee \ncharges settled via your linked payment method. \n(c) You are responsible for regularly reviewing your session history in the Metre App. If \nyou discover any discrepancies regarding recorded parking duration or fee calculations, \nyou must notify us via the Metre App or customer support (see Condition 20) within 30 \ndays of the relevant parking session date. \n14.2. Retention and Confidentiality of Records \n(a) All session logs and transaction records generated by your On-Loan MetreTag and the \nMetre App will be securely maintained in our digital systems. \n(b) We treat all session and billing data as confidential. Save for displaying records to \nyou within the Metre App, we will only disclose your transaction records to: \n(i) Participating car park operators or managers displaying the Metre acceptance logo \n(solely to the extent necessary to verify premises access, validate session timestamps, \nor resolve disputed parking charges); \n\n(ii) Our authorized third-party contractors, cloud infrastructure providers, and payment \nprocessing partners (such as FPS execution gateways) who are bound by strict \nobligations of confidentiality and provide essential services for our operations; \n(iii) Law enforcement agencies, courts, or regulatory authorities in Hong Kong to satisfy \na legally binding search warrant, court order, or statutory requirement; or \n(iv) Legal counsel or debt recovery agencies in the event of default or unpaid parking \nfees, subject to Section 10 and applicable data privacy laws.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-14","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 14","text":"15. New Services \nWe may introduce new features, services, or functionality associated with your On-Loan \nMetreTag and/or the Metre App from time to time. Your use of any such new services will \nbe governed by these Conditions of Issue or by specific supplemental terms announced \nat the time of feature launch within the Metre App.\n16. Fees and Charges \nDetails of all applicable deposits, delivery fees, reactivation charges, and administrative \nfees are set out in our Schedule of Fees and Guidelines, accessible directly within the \nMetre App and on our official website at www.metre.hk. You are advised to review the \nlatest Schedule of Fees and Guidelines regularly.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-15","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 15","text":"17. Amendments to these Conditions of Issue \n17.1. Notice of Amendments: We reserve the right to amend these Conditions of Issue \nat any time. If an amendment affects fees, charges, or customer liabilities/obligations, \nwe will notify you by publishing a notice within the Metre App and on our official website \nat www.metre.hk. Any such notice shall specifically identify and summarize the \nmaterial changes being made. \n17.2. Effective Date: Any modifications will take effect on a date specified in the notice, \nwhich will be no less than 30 days after the date of publication in the Metre App or on \nour website. \n17.3. Binding Effect: Continued use of your MetreTag or the Metre App following the \neffective date of any amendment constitutes your full acceptance of the revised \nConditions of Issue. If you do not agree to the proposed changes, you must return your \nOn-Loan MetreTag and cancel your Metre App account prior to the effective date \npursuant to Section 10.1. \n17.4. Latest Version: The most current version of these Conditions of Issue is always \navailable for inspection within the Metre App settings and on our official website. \n17.5. Deposit Refund on Amendment-Related Cancellation: If you choose to cancel \nyour Metre App account and return your On-Loan MetreTag solely as a result of \n\namendments to these Conditions of Issue pursuant to Condition 17.3, you will receive a \nfull refund of your Deposit without any deductions for handling or administrative \ncharges, provided all outstanding parking fees have been settled in full. \n17.6. Sessions in Progress: Any amendments to these Conditions of Issue shall not \naffect the terms applicable to parking sessions already in progress at the time the \namendments take effect.\n18. Rights of Third Parties \nThese Conditions of Issue are between you and Metre Hong Kong Limited. No third party \nshall have any right to enforce or rely on any provision of these Conditions of Issue \nunder the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Ordinance (Cap. 623) or otherwise, save for \npermitted successors and assigns.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-16","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 16","text":"19. Force Majeure \n19.1. We shall not be liable for any delay or failure in performing our obligations under \nthese Conditions of Issue where such delay or failure arises from causes beyond our \nreasonable control. Such causes include, without limitation: acts of God, extreme \nweather or climatic conditions, power failures, cellular or satellite network outages, \ninternet backbone disruptions, physical gate/hardware failures at third-party car parks, \ntrade disputes, or changes in applicable laws or government regulations. \n19.2. If a force majeure event continues for more than 90 days, either party may \nterminate these Conditions of Issue by written notice, and we will refund any \noutstanding Deposit balance.\n20. Communication and Support \n20.1. Official Channels: All questions, session discrepancies, lost tag reports, or \nsupport requests must be submitted via WhatsApp at (852) 5911 7372, by email \nto support@metre.hk, or via official support channels listed at www.metre.hk. \n20.2. Communications from Us: All notices, billing alerts, and official communications \nfrom us will be sent via in-app push notifications or to the email address associated \nwith your Metre App account. Communications received through any other unverified \nchannel should be treated as unauthorized. \n20.3. Third-Party Authorization: If a third party purports to contact us on your behalf, we \nreserve the right to request written authorization or contact you directly via your \nregistered email to verify identity before acting on any instructions.\n21. Governing Language \nThese Conditions of Issue may be translated into Chinese or other languages for \nreference purposes only. In the event of any discrepancy, ambiguity, or inconsistency \n\nbetween the English version and any translated version, the English version shall strictly \nprevail.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"conditions-17","title":"Conditions of Issue of MetreTag (MetreTag 發行及使用條件) — section 17","text":"22. Governing Law and Jurisdiction \nThese Conditions of Issue shall be governed by, and construed in accordance with, the \nlaws of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. You and Metre Hong Kong Limited \nirrevocably agree that the courts of Hong Kong shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle \nany dispute or claim (contractual or non-contractual) arising out of or in connection \nwith these Conditions of Issue.","keywords":["conditions","發行","使用條件","metretag","deposit","按金","parking","泊車","fee","費用","buffer","額度","malfunction","故障","return","退回","cancellation","取消","loss","遺失","tamper","篡改","liability","責任"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-1","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 1","text":"Metre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 1 of 9 \nMETRE HONG KONG LIMITED \nPRIVACY POLICY STATEMENT \nEffective Date: 6 Aug 2026 \nVersion: 1.0 \n \nSUMMARY OF THIS PRIVACY POLICY STATEMENT \nThis summary highlights the key points of our privacy practices for your convenience. It is not a \nsubstitute for the full Privacy Policy Statement below, which you should read in full and which \nprevails over this summary in the event of any inconsistency. \n• What we collect: your name and contact details, payment/settlement identifiers, MetreTag and \ndevice identifiers, and MetreTag usage/parking session data. We do not collect credit or debit card \nnumbers, and we do not use cookies, tracking technologies, or SDKs to collect data (paragraphs 4–\n5). \n• Why we use it: to issue and manage your MetreTag, operate our parking access and payment \nsystems, provide customer support, and meet our legal and compliance obligations (paragraph 6). \n• Marketing: we only send marketing communications with your explicit consent, and you can opt \nout at any time, free of charge (paragraphs 7–8). \n• Who we share it with: infrastructure and technical service providers, participating parking \noperators, operational contractors, our affiliates, and regulators or law enforcement where legally \nrequired — all within Hong Kong (paragraph 9). \n• How long we keep it: only for as long as necessary, after which it is erased or anonymized \n(paragraphs 11–13). \n• Security: we apply technical, organizational, and managerial safeguards to protect your data \n(paragraphs 14–16). \n• Children: our services are not intended for, and we do not knowingly collect data from, persons \nunder 18 (paragraph 17). \n• Data breaches: we are committed to notifying affected users and the Privacy Commissioner for \nPersonal Data of a significant data breach (paragraph 18). \n• Automated decisions: certain fraud-prevention decisions may be automated; you may request \nhuman review (paragraph 19). \n• Your rights: access, correction, opt-out of marketing, and complaint to the Privacy Commissioner \nfor Personal Data (see the summary table and paragraphs 20–25). \n \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 2 of 9 \nTABLE OF CONTENTS \nSUMMARY OF THIS PRIVACY POLICY STATEMENT .................................................................. 1 \nGENERAL ............................................................................................................................................... 3 \nDEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION ............................................................................................ 3 \nOUR COMPANY POLICY .................................................................................................................... 3 \nSTATEMENT OF PRACTICES ............................................................................................................. 4 \nTYPES OF PERSONAL DATA COLLECTED AND HELD............................................................ 4 \nCOOKIES, TRACKING TECHNOLOGIES AND SDK DATA ....................................................... 4 \nPURPOSES OF KEEPING PERSONAL DATA................................................................................ 5 \nUSE OF PERSONAL DATA IN DIRECT MARKETING ................................................................ 5 \nDISCLOSURE OF PERSONAL DATA ............................................................................................. 6 \nACCURACY AND RETENTION OF PERSONAL DATA .............................................................. 6 \nSECURITY OF PERSONAL DATA .................................................................................................. 7 \nCHILDREN'S PERSONAL DATA .................................................................................................... 7 \nDATA BREACH NOTIFICATION .................................................................................................... 7 \nAUTOMATED DECISION-MAKING ............................................................................................... 7 \nACCESS, CORRECTION AND OTHER RIGHTS ........................................................................... 8 \nLINKS TO OTHER WEBSITES ............................................................................................................ 8 \nAMENDMENTS TO THIS PRIVACY POLICY STATEMENT .......................................................... 9 \nINTERNAL COMPLIANCE PRACTICES ............................................................................................ 9 \nGOVERNING LANGUAGE .................................................................................................................. 9 \nCONDITIONS OF ISSUE ....................................................................................................................... 9 \n \n \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 3 of 9 \nGENERAL","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-2","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 2","text":"1. Metre Hong Kong Limited (the \"Company\", \"we\", \"our\" or \"us\"), the issuer of the MetreTag \nand operator of the Metre App and associated platforms, respects the privacy of its users and \nrecognizes the importance of protecting personal data. We collect and process personal data \nto efficiently provide our vehicle access, parking session tracking, and transaction settlement \nservices to our customers. This Privacy Policy Statement is designed to help you understand \nwhat information the Company collects, how we use and safeguard that information, and your \nrights regarding your personal data. \nDEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-3","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 3","text":"2. In this Privacy Policy Statement, unless the context otherwise requires: \n\"Ordinance\" means the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (Cap. 486) of the Laws of the \nHong Kong Special Administrative Region; \n\"Personal Data\" means any personal data held by the Company that falls within the \nfollowing categories, in each case to the extent that it constitutes “personal data” under \nsection 2(1) of the Ordinance: \n(a) Identity and Registration Data — information provided by an applicant, account \nholder, or registered user of the Metre App or MetreTag, and information relating to \npersons linked to a Service Provider or commercial partner applicant (including \nbeneficial owners, directors, and officers of corporate entities), whether contained in \nregistration forms or submitted via the Metre App; \n(b) Session Data — data and records collected during your use of the MetreTag, \nincluding parking session entry and exit timestamps, physical locations, and session \nduration data captured by our Metre readers or integrated hardware systems; \n(c) Account and Payment Data — data and records collected during the operation and \nuse of the Metre App and payment processing services, including linked payment \ndetails, account transaction logs, and device identifiers; and \n(d) Device Data — information relating to the mobile device(s) used to access the Metre \nApp, as further described in paragraph 4(f) below; \n\"Service Provider\" means any car park operator, property manager, access control operator, \nor mobility service provider that utilizes the Metre system to record parking sessions, grant \nvehicle access, or manage parking premises, and has been approved by us. Service Providers \nwill clearly display the Metre acceptance logo at their physical locations, access barriers, or \nwithin online channels. \nOUR COMPANY POLICY","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-4","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 4","text":"3. We pledge to comply fully with, and where reasonably practicable exceed, the requirements \nof the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (Cap. 486) of Hong Kong. In fulfilling this pledge, \nwe commit to: \n(i) Collect adequate, but not excessive, Personal Data by lawful and fair means solely \nfor lawful purposes directly related to our vehicle access, parking session tracking, \npayment settlement, and account administration operations; \n(ii) Take all reasonably practicable steps to ensure that all Personal Data collected or \nretained by us is accurate and kept up to date, having regard to the purposes for \nwhich it is used; \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 4 of 9 \n(iii) Refrain from using Personal Data where there are reasonable grounds for believing \nthat the data is inaccurate or outdated, having regard to the specified operational \npurposes; \n(iv) Erase or securely anonymize Personal Data when it is no longer necessary for the \nfulfillment of the purposes for which it was collected; \n(v) Use Personal Data strictly for the purposes specified at the time of collection, unless \nyou have given your express prior consent for a change of use, or such use is \nrequired or permitted by the Ordinance or applicable laws of Hong Kong; \n(vi) Implement appropriate technical, physical, and organizational security measures to \nprotect Personal Data against unauthorized or accidental access, processing, erasure, \nloss, or other misuse; \n(vii) Ensure you are informed of the kinds of Personal Data we hold and the primary \npurposes for which your data will be processed; and \n(viii) Provide you with rights of access to and correction of your Personal Data held by us \nin accordance with the Ordinance. \nWe reserve the right to charge a reasonable administrative fee as permitted under the \nOrdinance for processing formal data access requests. \nSTATEMENT OF PRACTICES \nTYPES OF PERSONAL DATA COLLECTED AND HELD","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-5","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 5","text":"4. For the purpose of conducting the Company's business (including operating the Metre App, \nprocessing vehicle access, and settling parking transactions), we may collect from you and \nhold some or all of the following Personal Data (depending on the specific products, features, \nor services you select) to enable us to issue your MetreTag and provide our services to you: \na. Your name; \nb. Contact details, including email address, and delivery or mailing address (for \nMetreTag dispatch and official correspondence); \nc. Payment and settlement information, including designated FPS (Faster Payment \nSystem) identifiers, proxy IDs, or bank account details for processing deposit refunds \nor transaction settlements. We do not collect or store credit or debit card numbers; \nd. Your MetreTag identifier, hardware serial number, and cryptographic binding keys \nassociated with your account; \ne. MetreTag usage and session data, including parking entry/exit timestamps, session \nduration, physical car park locations, and barrier interactions1; \nf. Mobile device information, including unique device identifiers (e.g., IDFV/UUID), \noperating system version, and device parameters where the Metre App is installed; \ng. Customer support records, including app activity logs, feedback submissions, and \ncommunication history between you and our support channels. \nCOOKIES, TRACKING TECHNOLOGIES AND SDK DATA \n \n1Such usage and session data is Personal Data only to the extent that it can, directly or indirectly, be \nused to ascertain your identity. \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 5 of 9\n5. We do not use cookies, web beacons, tracking pixels, software development kits (SDKs), or \nsimilar tracking technologies to collect Personal Data through the Metre App or our website. \nIf this changes in the future, we will update this Privacy Policy Statement accordingly and, \nwhere required by the Ordinance, obtain your consent beforehand. \nPURPOSES OF KEEPING PERSONAL DATA","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-6","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 6","text":"6. Personal Data held by us may be used for any of the following purposes (as applicable): \na. Processing your account registration and orders for On-Loan MetreTags; \nb. Managing, operating, and maintaining the Metre parking access system, Metre App, \nand hardware infrastructure, including processing entry/exit barrier clearance and \ncalculating session fees; \nc. Verifying your MetreTag serials, payment credentials, and app activity records; \nd. Processing payment settlements, collecting outstanding parking fees, and managing \nFPS Deposit transfers or refunds; \ne. Sending you operational communications, including real-time parking session \nnotifications, fee statements, system alerts, and customer support messages; \nf. Providing you with direct marketing materials and promotions (subject to your \nexplicit consent as set out in paragraph 8); \ng. Enforcing our legal rights under the Conditions of Issue, including investigating \nimproper use, non-payment, or unreturned On-Loan MetreTags; \nh. Conducting customer due diligence, risk assessments, and compliance checks as \nrequired by applicable laws, rules, or guidelines in Hong Kong; \ni. Designing new products or improving existing hardware, firmware, mobile \napplications, and parking ecosystem services provided by us, our subsidiaries, and \nour affiliates, based on the analysis of anonymized and/or aggregated data that does \nnot identify you; \nj. Investigating customer complaints, technical glitches, hardware malfunctions, or \nsuspicious transaction activities; \nk. Preventing, detecting, or investigating fraud, unauthorized device modification, or \ncriminal activities; and \nl. Disclosing information as required by any applicable laws, court orders, regulatory \nauthorities, or law enforcement requests within the Hong Kong Special \nAdministrative Region. \nUSE OF PERSONAL DATA IN DIRECT MARKETING","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-7","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 7","text":"7. We intend to use your Personal Data to send you direct marketing communications regarding \nour products, services, special promotions, and offers relating to parking and mobility \nservices: \na. Data Used: Your name, email address, and mobile device identifiers (for in-app push \nnotifications). We do not collect or use telephone numbers for direct marketing \npurposes; \nb. Delivery Channels: Email and push notifications delivered through the Metre App; \nc. Consent Required: We will not use your Personal Data for direct marketing \npurposes unless we have received your explicit prior consent. You may opt out or \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 6 of 9 \nobject to our use of your Personal Data for direct marketing at any time, free of \ncharge, via the settings in the Metre App or by notifying us through our designated \nsupport channels.\n8. Only with your explicit consent as described above will we use your Personal Data to provide \nyou with tailored marketing materials and offers relating to Metre products and services. To \nachieve this, we may carry out internal operational and analytical procedures to: \na. Better understand your usage patterns and preferences to provide services better \ntailored to your needs (such as offering location-based or frequent-parker \npromotions); \nb. Assist us in selecting features, parking options, and mobility products that are likely \nto be of interest to you; and \nc. Arrange exclusive marketing offers, rewards, and user benefits within the Metre \necosystem. \nDISCLOSURE OF PERSONAL DATA","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-8","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 8","text":"9. All Personal Data held by us will be kept confidential. However, for the purposes set out in \nparagraphs 6 and 7 above, we may transfer or disclose such Personal Data to the following \nparties within Hong Kong: \na. Infrastructure & Technical Service Providers: Third-party cloud service providers, \nIT system hosts, software developers, and database management contractors bound \nby a duty of confidentiality to us; \nb. Parking Operators: Participating car park owners, operators, and property \nmanagement companies bound by a duty of confidentiality to us, solely to the extent \nnecessary to verify vehicle entry/exit, clear access barriers, and resolve session \ndiscrepancies; \nc. Operational Contractors: Our agents, contractors, and service providers who owe a \nduty of confidentiality to us and provide administrative, logistics/courier (for \nMetreTag delivery), payment execution (such as FPS gateway providers), debt \ncollection (in the event of overdue parking fees), legal, auditing, or customer support \nservices in connection with our business operations; \nd. Affiliates: Our subsidiaries and direct holding company which owe a duty of \nconfidentiality to us for internal management and service execution; and \ne. Regulatory & Legal Authorities: Any law enforcement agencies, government \nbodies, regulatory authorities, or courts of law in Hong Kong to whom we, our \nsubsidiaries, or our affiliates are under a legally binding obligation or court order to \nsatisfy a disclosure demand under applicable laws and regulations.\n10. For the avoidance of doubt, we will not transfer or disclose your Personal Data to any third \nparty (including our subsidiaries or affiliates) for use in direct marketing by that third party \nunless we have received your explicit prior written or in-app consent. \nACCURACY AND RETENTION OF PERSONAL DATA\n11. Personal Data collected and maintained by the Company shall be as accurate, complete, and \nup-to-date as is necessary for the performance of our parking access and transaction \nsettlement services.","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-9","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 9","text":"12. Personal Data will not be retained longer than necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it \nwas collected. Data that is no longer required will be erased, unless retention is required under \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 7 of 9 \napplicable Hong Kong laws or public interest mandates. For statistical or technical \nperformance analysis, records will be anonymized so that individual users cannot be \nidentified.\n13. We destroy records containing Personal Data in accordance with our internal security \nprocedures. Physical paper records will be destroyed by irreversible means, and electronic \nstorage media containing user data or hardware identifiers will be purged or sanitized prior to \ndisposal. \nSECURITY OF PERSONAL DATA\n14. We prioritize data security and implement appropriate technical, organizational, and \nmanagerial safeguards to protect your Personal Data against unauthorized or accidental \naccess, processing, loss, or erasure.\n15. Our cloud infrastructure, databases, and APIs are protected by industry-standard firewalls, \nencrypted connections (TLS/HTTPS), and hardware-level cryptographic controls. As standard \nemail transmissions are not fully secure, sensitive personal credentials or verification \ndocuments should only be submitted through secure upload mechanisms within the Metre \nApp or designated support channels.\n16. Unnecessary or obsolete account data will be purged from our active systems in accordance \nwith our internal retention schedules. \nCHILDREN'S PERSONAL DATA\n17. The Metre App and our services are not intended for, or directed at, persons under the age of \n18, and we do not knowingly collect Personal Data from persons under the age of 18. If we \nbecome aware that we have inadvertently collected Personal Data from a person under the age \nof 18 without the necessary consent, we will take reasonable steps to delete that data as soon \nas practicable. If you believe that a person under the age of 18 has provided us with Personal \nData, please contact our Data Protection Officer using the contact details set out in paragraph \n25 below. \nDATA BREACH NOTIFICATION","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-10","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 10","text":"18. While the Ordinance does not currently impose a mandatory requirement on us to notify \naffected individuals or the Privacy Commissioner for Personal Data (“PCPD”) of a data \nbreach, we are committed to good practice in this area, having regard to the PCPD's Guidance \non Data Breach Handling and the Giving of Breach Notifications. In the event of a data \nbreach involving your Personal Data that poses a real risk of harm to you, we will, as soon as \nreasonably practicable: (a) take immediate steps to contain the breach and mitigate any \nresulting harm; (b) assess the cause, extent, and impact of the breach; and (c) notify affected \nusers, and, where appropriate, the PCPD, of the breach and of the steps we have taken or \nintend to take in response, in line with applicable best practice. \nAUTOMATED DECISION-MAKING","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-11","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 11","text":"19. In limited circumstances, we may use automated tools or systems to support decisions that \naffect you — for example, algorithmic checks used to detect suspected fraud or unauthorized \nuse of a MetreTag or account (see paragraph 6(k) above), which may result in a temporary \nsuspension of your account or MetreTag pending further review. Where an automated \ndecision has a legal or otherwise significant effect on you, you may request that a member of \nour staff review that decision by contacting our Data Protection Officer using the contact \ndetails set out in paragraph 25 below, and we will give you the opportunity to present your \nviews before a final decision is made. \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 8 of 9 \nACCESS, CORRECTION AND OTHER RIGHTS \nSummary of Your Rights \nYour Right What It Means How To Exercise It \nAccess \nRequest a copy of the \nPersonal Data we hold about \nyou \nSubmit the PCPD's prescribed Data Access \nRequest Form with proof of identity to our Data \nProtection Officer (paragraph 20) \nCorrection Ask us to correct inaccurate Personal Data Contact our Data Protection Officer (paragraph 22) \nOpt-out of \nDirect \nMarketing \nStop receiving marketing \ncommunications, free of \ncharge, at any time \nUse the settings in the Metre App, or contact our \nsupport channels or Data Protection Officer \n(paragraph 21) \nComplaint to \nthe PCPD \nRaise a concern if you believe \nwe have mishandled your \nPersonal Data \nContact our Data Protection Officer, or lodge a \ncomplaint with the Privacy Commissioner for \nPersonal Data at www.pcpd.org.hk (paragraph \n24)\n20. You have the right to request access to any Personal Data we hold about you. To submit a \nData Access Request, please complete the prescribed form issued by the Privacy \nCommissioner for Personal Data (PCPD) and send it, along with proof of identity, to our Data \nProtection Officer at the address set out in paragraph 25 below or via dpo@metre.hk. We may \ncharge a reasonable fee permitted under the Ordinance to cover administrative costs for \nprocessing your request.","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-12","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 12","text":"21. You have the right to object to or opt out of our use of your Personal Data for direct \nmarketing purposes at any time, free of charge. You can manage your preferences directly in \nthe Metre App settings or by notifying us via our official support channels.\n22. You have the right to request the correction of any inaccurate Personal Data held by us by \ncontacting our Data Protection Officer.\n23. We will comply with your data access or correction request unless we are required or \npermitted to refuse the request under the Ordinance or other applicable legal grounds.\n24. If you believe that we have handled your Personal Data in a manner inconsistent with this \nPrivacy Policy Statement or the Ordinance, we encourage you to contact our Data Protection \nOfficer in the first instance (see paragraph 25 below) so that we may investigate and address \nyour concerns. You also have the right to lodge a complaint directly with the Office of the \nPrivacy Commissioner for Personal Data, Hong Kong (Hotline: 2827 2827; Website: \nwww.pcpd.org.hk), which independently oversees compliance with the Ordinance.\n25. Data Protection Officer Contact: \nEmail: dpo@metre.hk \nWebsite: www.metre.hk \nAddress: Flat 1229, Kai Fai House, Choi Wan (II) Estate, Kowloon, Hong Kong \nLINKS TO OTHER WEBSITES \n\nMetre Hong Kong Limited – Privacy Policy Statement \nPage 9 of 9\n26. The Metre App and website may contain links to third-party services or external platforms. \nThis Privacy Policy Statement applies solely to our services. When navigating to third-party \nlinks, you should consult their respective privacy policies. \nAMENDMENTS TO THIS PRIVACY POLICY STATEMENT","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"privacy-13","title":"Privacy Policy Statement (私隱政策聲明) — section 13","text":"27. We keep this Privacy Policy Statement under regular review. Where we make any material \nchange to this Privacy Policy Statement, we will give you reasonable advance notice of not \nless than 30 days before the change takes effect, and will notify you by email and/or in-app \nnotification via the Metre App, in addition to posting the updated Privacy Policy Statement on \nour official website (www.metre.hk). Minor or non-material changes (for example, \ncorrections of typographical errors) may be made without prior notice. \nINTERNAL COMPLIANCE PRACTICES\n28. Our Data Protection Officer oversees compliance with the Ordinance within the Company. \nWe maintain the following internal measures: \na. Maintenance of a formal log book recording any refused data access or correction \nrequests and the specific legal grounds for refusal; \nb. Inclusion of a clear Personal Information Collection Statement (PICS) in our app \nonboarding and account registration workflows; and \nc. Implementation of internal privacy guidelines, data security protocols, and staff \ntraining to ensure alignment with up-to-date data protection standards. \nGOVERNING LANGUAGE\n29. In the event of any inconsistency or conflict between the English and Chinese versions of this \nPrivacy Policy Statement, the English version shall strictly prevail. \nCONDITIONS OF ISSUE\n30. Nothing in this Privacy Policy Statement shall limit or prejudice the rights and obligations of \nthe Company under the Metre Conditions of Issue.","keywords":["privacy","私隱","policy","政策","personal data","個人資料","collection","收集","use","使用","retention","保留","dar","查閱","correction","更正","pcs","pics"],"category":"legal","lang":"en"},{"id":"contact","title":"Contact us (聯絡我們)","text":"Metre customer service: support@metre.hk; phone / WhatsApp (852) 5911 7372; website www.metre.hk; office hours Monday to Saturday 09:00–21:00, closed on Sundays and public holidays. The Metre customer-service team is available 24/7 via the WhatsApp button on the website. For installation problems, contact support@metre.hk or call 5911 7372. Facebook: facebook.com/metrehk; Instagram: instagram.com/metrehk.","keywords":["contact","聯絡","support","支援","whatsapp","5911 7372","85259117372","email","電郵","電話","office hours","辦公時間","24/7","facebook","instagram"],"category":"contact","lang":"zh-Hant-HK"},{"id":"console-dashboard","title":"Metre Console — merchant dashboard (logged-in)","text":"The Metre Console (console.metre.hk) is the online management service for car-park operators. After signing in (for example the test merchant account test@shalev.eu.org), the dashboard shows: a header with the signed-in account and a Sign out button; a notice 'Need to update your car park pricing or install MetrePoint? Please use the WhatsApp button in the bottom right to contact our team.'; navigation items Dashboard, Settlements and Devices; Device Health; a CAR PARK / STATUS / ACCESS LIST panel; Today's Revenue; Total Traffic; and a Transaction History table with columns DATE & TIME, SESSION REF, TAG ID, LOCATION, AMOUNT (HKD), STATUS and DETAILS, plus Export CSV and date/status/keyword filters. The minimum payout is HK$800.00.","keywords":["console","控制台","dashboard","儀表板","settlements","結算","devices","裝置","device health","裝置健康","revenue","收入","traffic","流量","transaction","交易","access list","通行列表","payout","出糧","export csv","sign out","登出"],"category":"console","lang":"en"},{"id":"merchant-application","title":"Metre Console — Merchant Application steps","text":"New merchant accounts must complete a Merchant Application in the console before they are activated. The form has five steps: 1 General Info, 2 Bank Account, 3 Technical Contact, 4 Documents, 5 Review & Submit. Step 1 (General Information) asks for company details — Company Name (English), Company Name (Chinese), Business Registration No., Business Type, Registered Address, District and Website — and primary contact details (Full Name, Job Title, Email, Phone). The console banner says to complete all steps to activate the account.","keywords":["merchant","商戶","application","申請","activate","啟用","general info","公司","business registration","商業登記","bank account","銀行","technical contact","技術聯絡","documents","文件","review","提交","account","帳戶"],"category":"console","lang":"en"}]};
